  "text": "MedlinePlus Consumer Guide: Managing Tension Headaches | Publisher: US National Library of\nTension Headache Relief & Prevention\nTension headaches are often triggered by muscle tightness in the neck,\nshoulders, or jaw, stress, or eye strain.\nSelf-Care Comfort Measures: - Heat or Ice Therapy: Apply a warm compress\nor heating pad to neck muscles, or a cold pack to the forehead. - Muscle\nRelaxation: Perform gentle neck stretches and shoulder rolls. - Hydration:\nSip water steadily, especially after long work sessions or hot weather. -\nRest: Take a break from computer screens every 30-45 minutes.\nAyurveda Context: Traditional Ayurvedic approaches suggest warm forehead\ncompresses and temple massage with suitable carrier oils for mild tension\nrelief.\nPage 1 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
